  "name": "Blue Monster (Boston Red Sox)",
  "kind": "special",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "drawnOn": "A320",
  "description": "Fuselage: White upper fuselage; navy lower fuselage and belly, the split low along the side and sweeping up to the crown just ahead of the fin, a bright-blue stripe along it. Tail: Navy fin almost filled by a big red Red Sox sock (white outline, white stripes on the cuff near the top), its foot running forward along the fin root; a second red sock wraps the aft fuselage and tail cone round the aft door, with white patches. Engines: Navy with white 'jetblue.com', polished lips. Winglets: Red wingtip fences with a white 'B'. Titles: Navy 'jetBlue' forward with the round 'BOSTON RED SOX' logo just aft of it; 'BLUE MONSTER' in red varsity capitals along the lower right side under the wing; 'Blue Monster' small under the cockpit windows. Artwork: Red Sox sock logos, small ones on the lower fuselage.",
