  "notes": "Body split drawn from right-side photos (2023-07, 2025-03) and the left from behind (2023-05); the split's top end, where it meets the crown, is hidden by the wing in most shots (medium-low). 'BLUE MONSTER' and the small socks are drawn for the right side only: no photo used shows the lower left fuselage. Re-checked 2026-11-15: 'jetBlue' placed as on the standard (measured in metres on the A321neo N2017J and checked on A320s: x 0.174-0.356 of an A320, cap 1.57 m, lowercase 0.76 of the capitals); 'jetblue.com' on the A320's nacelle x 0.43-0.79 (read off N615JB and N627JB); the name under the cockpit given its length. The roundel moved aft to x 0.375 to sit just behind the title's end, as on the photos. 2026-11-27: the fin's red area redrawn as the socks' outline (was a block under a diagonal) and the sock mark placed over it from the 2023-03-12 left-side photo; the roundel made bigger (about the title's cap height) and centered on the windows, clear of the title's end. 2026-11-28: the socks' feet on the aft fuselage redrawn from the 2023-03-12 left-side photo (fitted to shapes/A320.json with tools/photo_trace.py): the front sock's foot round the top of the aft door with its white heel and toe, the rear sock's foot below the stabilizer down to the belly with its white toe, both in a white outline, the white line between the socks carried down from the fin. The right side (2025-03 from below) shows the same. Later the same day the fin's socks were redrawn as fin areas traced on the same fitted photo instead of a placed mark, so the fin and the body meet: the rear sock's leg along the leading edge in its white outline, the front sock's cuff with six white stripes and its leg in front, the white line between them carried down to the front sock's heel on the body. 2026-11-28: only the rear sock continues onto the body (round the aft door and down under the stabilizer to the belly); the front sock, with the striped cuff, ends on the fin, its foot along the root with a white heel and toe and a white line closing it."
}
